// Between Frontiers: changes of sovereignty from 1925-01-01 to 2025-12-31 at the resolution of
// the 870 map states (assets/map/provinces.ron). Contract: crates/bf-sim/src/borders.rs
// (BordersFile); design: docs/borders.pt-BR.md. Doubts, criteria and the changes below the state
// resolution: data/history/BORDERS.md.
//
// Reference for the scorecard only: nothing in the game fires a change by its date.
//
// Contract (one entry per change, ordered by date then `from`):
//   date      ISO date the change took effect (criterion per line in `note`).
//   kind      Transfer   states move between two existing countries (cession, annexation of
//                        part of a country, return);
//             Secession  states form a new or restored country (one line per heir);
//             Annexation a whole country ends inside another: `states` is [] and means every
//                        state `from` holds on that date (replay the list in order);
//             Status     no territory moves: `from` becomes a subject of `to`, or sovereign when
//                        `to` == `from` (occupation regimes included, see `occupier`);
//             Rename     same country, new name (`from` == `to`, new name in `note`).
//   states    map state keys that move whole; a state moves with the majority (largest share)
//             of its area.
//   partial   (state key, share) that changed hands only in part and did NOT move; shares from
//             modern_iso3_by_area when the line ends at a modern border, otherwise approximate
//             (flagged "approx." in `note` and listed in the notes file).
//   occupier  occupying power(s) at creation or during the status, comma-separated tags.
//   wikidata  Wikidata item (resolved from the first or designated Wikipedia page).
//   source    Wikipedia pages checked, then the Wikidata item and the property whose date
//             equals `date` (P571 inception, P576 dissolved, P580/P582 start/end, P585 point).
//   note      criterion, caveats; "puppet: true" marks client states; "de facto" marks
//             unrecognised or partially recognised control.
// Tags: the 1925 tag continues when the state continues in international law (SOV = USSR and
// then Russia, GER = Reich and then FRG, RAJ = British India and then India, YEM = Yemen,
// EGY = Egypt incl. the UAR years, restored LTU/LAT/EST/AUT/LUX/ETH/ALB reuse their tags).
// New states use their ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 code of 2025; dissolved ones ISO 3166-3 or customary
// codes (DDR, YMD, RVN, SCG, RHO); a suffix X marks a code that would clash with another entity
// (CZR Czech Republic vs CZE Czechoslovakia of 1925; SLK, MMRX, PHLX, VNMX, KHMX, LAOX for
// wartime client states whose ISO code belongs to the later state). No `Occupation` lines: zones
// are recorded in `occupier` (see notes).
// Licence: facts from Wikidata (CC0) and English Wikipedia (facts only, no text copied); this
// file follows the repository data licence (CC BY-SA 4.0).

